      "difficulty": "easy",
      "question": "Given two curves y=f(x) and y=g(x) where f(x) ≥ g(x) on [a, b], what is the formula for the area between them?",
      "answer_guide": "Area = ∫ from a to b of [f(x) - g(x)] dx.",
      "explanation": "Area is the integral of the upper curve minus the lower curve.",
